.TH SYS-MONITOR 1 "December 2025" "1.0" "Sys-Monitor Manual"

.SH NAME
sys-monitor \- CPU and RAM monitoring tool for Linux

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sys-monitor

.SH DESCRIPTION
Sys-Monitor is a Bash-based command-line monitoring tool designed for Linux systems.
It displays real-time information about system resource usage, including CPU usage,
RAM usage, and lists of top processes consuming CPU and memory.

The program runs continuously in the terminal until interrupted by the user.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display version information and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.B sys-monitor
.RS
Run the system monitor with default settings.
.RE

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /proc/stat
Provides CPU usage information.
.TP
.I /proc/meminfo
Provides memory usage information.

.SH AUTHOR
Sys-Monitor Project Team

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR top (1),
.BR htop (1),
.BR free (1),
.BR ps (1)
